---
import ToolPage from '../../../layouts/ToolPage.astro';

const steps = [
  'Paste the address of the site you’re about to launch.',
  'We read the page the way Google and social apps do, then look for robots.txt, a sitemap, a favicon, and what happens on a page that doesn’t exist.',
  'Each item is green, amber or red with a one-line fix. Copy one prompt with every fix and paste it into Claude Code, Cursor or Codex.',
];

const faq = [
  { q: 'What does the launch checker look at?', a: 'Page title, description, share preview tags, favicon, https, the phone viewport tag, whether the page hides itself from Google, robots.txt, a sitemap, whether missing pages return a real 404, and image alt text. If your page is an empty shell filled in by JavaScript, it tells you that too.' },
  { q: 'What do green, amber and red mean?', a: 'Green is done. Amber works but is worth fixing before you share the link widely. Red will hurt you on launch day, like a starter title in Google results, links that show up without a picture, or a page that tells Google not to list it.' },
  { q: 'Why does my title say “still the starter text”?', a: 'Tools like Vite, Create Next App, Lovable and v0 ship with placeholder titles such as “Vite + React + TS”. They’re easy to miss because you rarely look at the browser tab, but they’re what Google shows.' },
  { q: 'Why does a missing page need to return 404?', a: 'Many single-page apps show the home page with a “200 OK” status for any address. Google can then list junk addresses, and broken links look like they work. A real 404 status fixes both.' },
  { q: 'Can I check a site on localhost?', a: 'No. We check from the internet, so the site needs a public address. Deploy a preview (Vercel, Netlify and Cloudflare all make one per branch), then paste that.' },
  { q: 'Does it check every page?', a: 'It checks the one address you paste, plus the site-wide files next to it. Run it on your home page first, then on any page you plan to share.' },
];
---
<ToolPage
  slug="launch-checker"
  title="Launch checker: is my site ready to launch? · Darnly"
  description="Paste your site to check the launch basics: title, description, share preview, favicon, https, robots.txt, sitemap, 404 page, phone viewport and alt text. Get a fix for each and one prompt for your AI agent."
  h1="Launch checker: is my site ready to launch?"
  lede="Paste your site and get a green, amber or red checklist of the launch basics people forget, each with a one-line fix and a prompt for your AI agent."
  steps={steps}
  faq={faq}
>
  <div class="lc">
    <form id="lc-form" class="ask">
      <label class="sr" for="lc-url">Website address</label>
      <input id="lc-url" type="text" inputmode="url" autocomplete="url" placeholder="yoursite.com" required />
      <button id="lc-go" type="submit">Check my site</button>
    </form>
    <p class="error" id="lc-error" role="alert" hidden></p>

    <div id="lc-out" hidden>
      <div class="summary">
        <div>
          <p class="verdict" id="lc-verdict"></p>
          <p class="counts" id="lc-counts"></p>
        </div>
        <button id="lc-prompt" type="button" class="primary">Copy all fixes for your AI agent</button>
      </div>
      <ul class="list" id="lc-list"></ul>
      <p class="note" id="lc-note" hidden></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</ToolPage>

<script>
  import '../../../scripts/launch-checker';
</script>

<style>
  .lc [hidden] { display: none !important; }
  .lc { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 20px; }
  .sr { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0 0 0 0); }
  .ask { display: flex; gap: 10px; }
  .ask input { flex: 1; min-width: 0; font: inherit; font-size: 18px; padding: 14px 18px; border: 2px solid var(--line); border-radius: 999px; background: var(--white); }
  .ask input:focus { outline: none; border-color: var(--sky); }
  .ask button { font: 600 16px/1 var(--body); padding: 0 26px; border: 0; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--sky); color: var(--white); cursor: pointer; white-space: nowrap; }
  .ask button:disabled { opacity: 0.6; cursor: wait; }
  .error { margin: 0; color: #B4234F; }

  .summary { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px 20px; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; }
  .verdict { margin: 0; font: 700 24px/1.2 var(--display); }
  .counts { margin: 4px 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; }
  .primary { font: 600 15px/1 var(--body); padding: 12px 18px; border: 0; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--ink); color: var(--white); cursor: pointer; }

  .list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 10px; }
  .list :global(.item) { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 28px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 4px 14px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left-width: 5px; border-radius: 14px; padding: 16px 18px; background: var(--white); }
  .list :global(.item.pass) { border-left-color: #1F9D55; }
  .list :global(.item.warn) { border-left-color: #E0A100; }
  .list :global(.item.fail) { border-left-color: #D2344F; }
  .list :global(.dot) { grid-row: span 3; width: 28px; height: 28px; border-radius: 50%; display: grid; place-items: center; font: 700 15px/1 var(--body); color: var(--white); }
  .list :global(.pass .dot) { background: #1F9D55; }
  .list :global(.warn .dot) { background: #E0A100; }
  .list :global(.fail .dot) { background: #D2344F; }
  .list :global(.label) { margin: 2px 0 0; font: 600 18px/1.3 var(--body); }
  .list :global(.detail) { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .list :global(.fix) { margin: 4px 0 0; font-size: 15px; }
  .list :global(.fix b) { font-weight: 600; }
  .list :global(.actions) { grid-column: 2; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .list :global(.actions a), .list :global(.actions button) { font: 600 14px/1 var(--body); padding: 9px 14px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--white); color: var(--ink); cursor: pointer; text-decoration: none; }
  .list :global(.actions a:hover), .list :global(.actions button:hover) { border-color: var(--sky); }
  .note { margin: 0; font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
</style>
